{"toolCallId":"call_9b055bd717d44bf09cf2983277e251ce","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n<!-- FILL: Keep the prefix table and add the two shell variables this task list uses. GOOD: `S` is the script path. `P` is the packet path. WEAK: Variables are defined below. -->\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n<!-- FILL: Replace the sample tasks with the real setup steps. Each task names a file and a verify command. GOOD: T001 Read the output block in `recommend-level.sh`. Verify: `rg -n 'Recommended Level'` prints one line. WEAK: T001 Set up the project. -->\n\n- [ ] T001 Create project structure\n- [ ] T002 Install dependencies\n- [ ] T003 [P] Configure development tools\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n<!-- FILL: Write one implementation task per file change. Add a `Verify:` line with the command and its expected output. GOOD: T002 Add the `--quiet` branch. Verify: `--quiet` prints one line. WEAK: T002 Implement the feature. -->\n\n- [ ] T004 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 1]\n- [ ] T005 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 2]\n- [ ] T006 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 3]\n- [ ] T007 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Add error handling]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n<!-- FILL: Write one verification task per requirement. Each one runs a command. GOOD: T003 Run both invocations. Verify: `wc -l` prints 1 and 17. WEAK: T003 Test everything. -->\n\n- [ ] T008 Test happy path manually\n- [ ] T009 Test edge cases\n- [ ] T010 Update documentation\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n<!-- FILL: Keep the three completion lines and add the one artifact that proves the phase is done. GOOD: `--quiet` prints one line and the suite passes. WEAK: Work is complete. -->\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n<!-- FILL: Name the spec and plan files. Add the decision record when the packet has one. GOOD: Specification: `spec.md`. Plan: `plan.md`. WEAK: See the other docs. -->\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n<!-- FILL: Fill each checklist section below. -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n<!-- FILL: Keep the three rows and add the rule this packet uses for a blocked task. GOOD: P0 blocks close. P1 needs a recorded reason. WEAK: Follow the priorities. -->\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per setup fact, each with a command. GOOD: CHK-001 [P0] The start commit is in `goal.md` section 4. WEAK: Setup is ready. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per file rule. A command must answer it. GOOD: CHK-010 [P0] `bash -n recommend-level.sh` exits 0. WEAK: Code is clean. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] Code passes lint/format checks\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No console errors or warnings\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Error handling implemented\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] Code follows project patterns\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per acceptance criterion. GOOD: CHK-020 [P0] `--quiet` prints one line. WEAK: Tests pass. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] Manual testing complete\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Edge cases tested\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Error scenarios validated\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n<!-- FILL: Keep this section, because every level requires it. Write one check per finding class this packet can produce. Delete only the rows that do not apply, never the section. GOOD: CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Every finding names one class. WEAK: All findings handled. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each actionable finding has a finding class: `instance-only`, `class-of-bug`, `cross-consumer`, `algorithmic`, `matrix/evidence`, or `test-isolation`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed, or instance-only status proven by grep.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed for changed helpers, policies, schema fields, response fields, docs, and tests.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] Security/path/parser/redaction fixes include adversarial table tests for delimiter, joined-input, outside-root, no-op, and fallback cases.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes and row count are listed before completion is claimed.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Hostile env/global-state variant executed when tests or code read process-wide state.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence is pinned to a fix SHA or explicit diff range, not a moving branch-relative range.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per security surface. Write `N/A` with a reason when none applies. GOOD: CHK-030 [P0] The script reads no credential. WEAK: Security is fine. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation implemented\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] Auth/authz working correctly\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per document that must agree. GOOD: CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md` and `tasks.md` name the same flag. WEAK: Docs are updated. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec/plan/tasks synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] Code comments adequate\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] README updated (if applicable)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per file location rule. GOOD: CHK-050 [P1] Test copies live under `scratch/test/`. WEAK: Files are organized. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Temp files in scratch/ only\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] scratch/ cleaned before completion\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n<!-- FILL: Count the boxes by priority and write the three totals. GOOD: P0 12, P1 13, P2 1. WEAK: Most items done. -->\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | [X] | [ ]/[X] |\n| P1 Items | [Y] | [ ]/[Y] |\n| P2 Items | [Z] | [ ]/[Z] |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-25\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per ADR, or delete the section when the packet records no ADR. GOOD: CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 is followed by T002. WEAK: Architecture is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] Architecture decisions documented in decision-record.md\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] All ADRs have status (Proposed/Accepted)\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives documented with rejection rationale\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] Migration path documented (if applicable)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per performance claim, or delete the section when the packet makes none. GOOD: CHK-110 [P1] The flag adds under 5 ms. WEAK: Performance is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] Response time targets met (NFR-P01)\n- [ ] CHK-111 [P1] Throughput targets met (NFR-P02)\n- [ ] CHK-112 [P2] Load testing completed\n- [ ] CHK-113 [P2] Performance benchmarks documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per deployment step, or delete the section when the packet ships no service. GOOD: CHK-120 [P0] The rollback command was run in a copy. WEAK: Ready to deploy. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure documented and tested\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P0] Feature flag configured (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-122 [P1] Monitoring/alerting configured\n- [ ] CHK-123 [P1] Runbook created\n- [ ] CHK-124 [P2] Deployment runbook reviewed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per compliance surface, or delete the section when none applies. GOOD: CHK-130 [P1] No license changed. WEAK: Compliance is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] Security review completed\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] Dependency licenses compatible\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] OWASP Top 10 checklist completed\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] Data handling compliant with requirements\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per document pair that must agree, or delete the section when the packet holds no paired documents. GOOD: CHK-140 [P1] `plan.md` and `tasks.md` agree on the three phases. WEAK: Docs are verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] API documentation complete (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Name the real approver for each role. Delete a row when the role does not exist. Write `N/A` or delete the section when no sign-off applies. GOOD: Conductor, runs every task. Operator, merges the commit. WEAK: Signed off. -->\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | Technical Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | Product Owner | [ ] Approved | |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | QA Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n**Task variables**: `S=\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\"` and `P=\"specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\"`. Set both in the shell before running a `Verify:` command.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the parser loop and both output functions (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'output_text|output_json|JSON_OUTPUT' \"$S\"` prints the global, both functions and the section 7 dispatch site.\n- [ ] T002 Capture the default report for the reference input (`$P/scratch/baseline-default.txt`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 > \"$P/scratch/baseline-default.txt\"; wc -l < \"$P/scratch/baseline-default.txt\"` prints 16.\n- [ ] T003 Record the reference recommendation line (`$P/scratch/baseline-default.txt`). Verify: `grep -c '^Recommended Level: 0 (Quick)$' \"$P/scratch/baseline-default.txt\"` prints 1.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add the `QUIET=false` global beside `JSON_OUTPUT` (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n '^QUIET=false$' \"$S\"` prints one line.\n- [ ] T005 Add the `--quiet` case to the argument parser (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet >/dev/null; echo $?` prints 0.\n- [ ] T006 Return after the recommendation line in `output_text()` when quiet mode is active (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet | wc -l` prints 1.\n- [ ] T007 Keep the recommendation line's text identical in both modes (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet` prints `Recommended Level: 0 (Quick)`.\n- [ ] T008 List `--quiet` in the header usage block and in `show_help()` (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help | grep -c -- '--quiet'` prints 1.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T009 Diff the default report against the captured baseline (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 | diff - \"$P/scratch/baseline-default.txt\"` prints nothing and exits 0.\n- [ ] T010 Confirm the JSON path ignores quiet (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 --json --quiet | wc -l` prints 36.\n- [ ] T011 Confirm quiet composes with `--no-recommend-phases` (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 --no-recommend-phases --quiet | wc -l` prints 1.\n- [ ] T012 Confirm quiet never suppresses an error (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet 2>&1 >/dev/null | grep -c 'At least --loc or --files'` prints 1.\n- [ ] T013 Syntax-check the edited script (`$S`). Verify: `bash -n \"$S\"; echo $?` prints 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed: both output forms read correctly in a terminal, and every row of `acceptance-criteria.md` is `Met`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Decision record**: `plan.md` carries ADR-001; this packet writes no separate `decision-record.md`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md. Verify: `rg -c '^\\| REQ-00' \"$P/spec.md\"` prints 5.\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md. Verify: `rg -c '^### Step|^## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES' \"$P/plan.md\"` prints at least 1.\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available. Verify: `command -v bash diff wc` names all three.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] Script parses cleanly. Verify: `bash -n \"$S\"; echo $?` prints 0.\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No stray debug output. Verify: `rg -n 'set -x|echo DEBUG' \"$S\"` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Error handling preserved: quiet never suppresses stderr. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet 2>&1 >/dev/null | grep -c 'ERROR'` prints 1.\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] Code follows the file's existing pattern: a global, a parser case, a renderer branch. Verify: `rg -n 'QUIET|JSON_OUTPUT' \"$S\"` shows the new global in the same block as the old one.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met. Verify: every row of `acceptance-criteria.md` reads `Met`.\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] Quiet prints exactly one line. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet | wc -l` prints 1.\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Default report unchanged. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 | diff - \"$P/scratch/baseline-default.txt\"` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Error and JSON paths tested. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 --json --quiet | wc -l` prints 36 and `bash \"$S\" --quiet` exits 1.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each actionable finding has a finding class: `instance-only`, `class-of-bug`, `cross-consumer`, `algorithmic`, `matrix/evidence`, or `test-isolation`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed: both output functions were read before the branch was added. Verify: `rg -n '^output_text\\(\\)|^output_json\\(\\)' \"$S\"` prints both.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed: every invocation of the script in the skill was checked for a `--quiet` expectation. Verify: `rg -n 'recommend-level.sh' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit | rg -c -- '--quiet'` prints 0 before this packet publishes the flag.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence is pinned to the packet's diff, not to a moving branch. Verify: the commit named in `implementation-summary.md` is the one holding the change.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets. Verify: `rg -n 'password|token|secret' \"$S\"` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation intact: the numeric checks still run before any renderer. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc abc --files 2 --quiet; echo $?` prints an error and 1.\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] No auth surface exists to regress. Verify: `rg -n 'curl|wget|http' \"$S\"` prints nothing.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec/plan/tasks synchronized on the flag's name and its one-line output. Verify: `rg -c -- '--quiet' \"$P/spec.md\" \"$P/plan.md\" \"$P/tasks.md\"` prints a non-zero count for each file.\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] Code comments adequate: the header usage block and `show_help()` both name the flag. Verify: `rg -c -- '--quiet' \"$S\"` prints at least 3.\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] No README or reference page needs an edit: every existing example invocation stays valid. Verify: `rg -n 'recommend-level.sh' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references | rg -c -- '--quiet'` prints 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Temp files live in `scratch/` only. Verify: `ls \"$P/scratch\"` lists the baseline and no stray copy of the script.\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` cleaned before completion, keeping only the baseline that the evidence cites. Verify: `ls \"$P/scratch\"` lists `baseline-default.txt` and `.gitkeep`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 13 | [ ]/13 |\n| P1 Items | 19 | [ ]/19 |\n| P2 Items | 12 | [ ]/12 |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-25\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 in `plan.md` is followed: quiet is read in `output_text()` only. Verify: `rg -n 'QUIET' \"$S\"` shows no reference inside `output_json()`.\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] The ADR carries a status. Verify: `rg -n '^\\*\\*Status\\*\\*: Proposed' \"$P/plan.md\"` prints one line.\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives are documented with a rejection rationale. Verify: `rg -n 'Alternatives Rejected' \"$P/plan.md\"` prints one line.\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] No migration path is needed: the change is additive and the default path is untouched. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 | diff - \"$P/scratch/baseline-default.txt\"` prints nothing.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] NFR-P01 holds: the quiet run stays under 100 ms. Verify: `time bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet >/dev/null` reports a real time below 0.1 s.\n- [ ] CHK-111 [P1] Quiet does less work than the report, never more: it returns before the breakdown prints. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet | wc -l` prints 1, which is fewer lines than the 16-line report.\n- [ ] CHK-112 [P2] No load test applies: the script is a single-shot CLI. Verify: `rg -n 'sleep|while true' \"$S\"` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-113 [P2] No benchmark is recorded: the only performance claim is NFR-P01, measured by CHK-110. Verify: `rg -n 'NFR-P01' \"$P/spec.md\"` prints one line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure documented in `plan.md` section 7 and in the L2 enhanced rollback. Verify: `rg -n 'Rollback Plan|Rollback Procedure' \"$P/plan.md\"` prints both headings.\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P1] No feature flag or rollout switch exists: `--quiet` is per-invocation. Verify: `rg -n 'feature.flag|rollout' \"$S\"` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-122 [P2] No monitoring surface exists: the script emits no metrics. Verify: `rg -n 'metrics|statsd|otel' \"$S\"` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-123 [P2] No runbook is needed: the rollback is one revert plus two commands. Verify: `rg -c '^[0-9]\\. ' \"$P/plan.md\"` counts the rollback steps that exist.\n- [ ] CHK-124 [P2] No deployment step exists: the script ships inside the skill tree. Verify: `rg -n 'deploy|release' \"$P/plan.md\"` prints no deployment action.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] No security review surface: the change adds no input parsing beyond a boolean flag. Verify: `rg -n 'eval|exec' \"$S\"` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] No dependency license changes: no package is added. Verify: `git diff --stat -- '*.json' 'package.json' 'package-lock.json'` prints nothing for this change.\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] No OWASP surface applies: the script reads no request, cookie or credential. Verify: `rg -n 'cookie|session|credential' \"$S\"` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] No data handling applies: the script persists nothing. Verify: `rg -n '> *[^&]|tee ' \"$S\"` prints no write outside stdout.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents agree on the flag's behaviour and the one-line output. Verify: `rg -c 'Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)' \"$P/spec.md\" \"$P/plan.md\"` prints a non-zero count for each file.\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P2] No API documentation exists to update: the script is a CLI, not a service. Verify: `rg -n 'openapi|swagger' \"$P\"` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] No user-facing page changes: the reference docs list usage examples that remain valid. Verify: `rg -n 'recommend-level.sh' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references | rg -c -- '--quiet'` prints 0.\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer is the help text itself. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help | rg -c -- '--quiet'` prints 1.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| N/A | Technical Lead | Not required: the packet is Draft and no implementation has run | |\n| N/A | Product Owner | Not required: the change is additive and the caller requested it | |\n| N/A | QA Lead | Not required: verification is the two output forms in `tasks.md` | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":66,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":87}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_9bd6b7bdfc4c409db79d8b4139882b98","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n<!-- FILL: Fill the stack row and write three sentences: what changes, where, and how you will prove it. GOOD: Change one bash script. Add one output branch. Prove it with a line count. WEAK: This plan describes the implementation. -->\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., TypeScript, Python 3.11] |\n| **Framework** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., React, FastAPI] |\n| **Storage** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., PostgreSQL, None] |\n| **Testing** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., Jest, pytest] |\n\n### Overview\n[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n<!-- FILL: Turn each gate into a check a command can answer. Keep the boxes unticked until they pass. GOOD: `rg -n 'quiet' recommend-level.sh` prints the new branch before the task starts. WEAK: The team agrees the plan is ready. -->\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Tests passing (if applicable)\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n<!-- FILL: Name the pattern in three words, then list the one component that changes. GOOD: Single script branch. The component is `recommend-level.sh`. WEAK: Standard architecture. -->\n\n### Pattern\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: MVC | MVVM | Clean Architecture | Serverless | Monolith | Other]\n\n### Key Components\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 1]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 2]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n\n### Data Flow\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description of how data moves through the system]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n<!-- FILL: Name each surface the change touches. Write `not a consumer` when it does not read the change. Write `N/A` or delete the whole addendum when no fix surface applies. GOOD: `recommend-level.sh`: owns the output. Action: update. WEAK: Various files. -->\n\nUse this section when `research_intent=fix_bug`, when planning from a deep-review FAIL/CONDITIONAL verdict, or when any finding touches security, path handling, env precedence, schema boundaries, persistence, public responses, or shared policy.\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: producer/helper/policy] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: what owns the behavior] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: grep/test/doc evidence] |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: consumer/status/docs/tests] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: how it observes the behavior] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: grep/test/doc evidence] |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `rg -n '<field|string|helper|literal|error-pattern>' <module-or-files>`.\n- Consumers of changed symbols: `rg -n '<changedSymbol>|<changedConstant>|<changedPublicField>' . --glob '*.ts' --glob '*.js' --glob '*.md'`.\n- Matrix axes: list every independent input axis and the required rows before implementation.\n- Algorithm invariant: for path/redaction/parser/resolver/security fixes, state the invariant and adversarial cases.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n<!-- FILL: Point to `tasks.md` and name the three phases in one line. GOOD: Setup reads the current output. Implementation adds the branch. Verification counts lines. WEAK: See tasks. -->\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n<!-- FILL: Name the one command you will run and the output it must print. GOOD: `--quiet` prints 1 line. The default prints 17. WEAK: Test it manually. -->\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Components/functions] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Jest/pytest/etc.] |\n| Integration | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: API endpoints/flows] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Tools] |\n| Manual | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: User journeys] | Browser |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: List each tool the change needs, or write `None`. GOOD: `bash` and `awk`. No new package. WEAK: Usual dependencies. -->\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: System/Library] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Internal/External] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Green/Yellow/Red] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Impact] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger and the one command that reverts the change. GOOD: Trigger: the default output changes. Revert the one commit. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\n- **Trigger**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Conditions requiring rollback]\n- **Procedure**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How to revert changes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: Draw the phase order in the fence, then fill the table with depends-on and blocks. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Setup to Implementation to Verification. Verification blocks close. WEAK: Phases depend on each other. -->\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──────┐\n                      ├──► Phase 2 (Core) ──► Phase 3 (Verify)\nPhase 1.5 (Config) ───┘\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Core, Config |\n| Config | Setup | Core |\n| Core | Setup, Config | Verify |\n| Verify | Core | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n<!-- FILL: Give each phase an estimate and a total. Mark the total as an assumption. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Setup 10 minutes, implementation 30, verification 10. Total 50 minutes. WEAK: A few hours. -->\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 1-2 hours] |\n| Core Implementation | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 4-8 hours] |\n| Verification | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 1-2 hours] |\n| **Total** | | **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 6-12 hours]** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger, the steps and the data reversal. Write `No` when no data changes. Delete the whole section when the packet ships no deployable service. GOOD: Trigger: default output changes. Steps: revert one commit, rerun the two commands. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [ ] Backup created (if data changes)\n- [ ] Feature flag configured\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Immediate action - e.g., disable feature flag]\n2. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Revert code - e.g., git revert or redeploy previous version]\n3. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Verify rollback - e.g., smoke test critical paths]\n4. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Notify stakeholders - if user-facing]\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Yes/No]\n- **Reversal procedure**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Steps or \"N/A\"]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n<!-- FILL: Draw the component order and fill the matrix with produces and blocks. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Script to test to close. WEAK: Components depend on each other. -->\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Setup     │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └──────┬──────┘     └─────────────┘\n                          │\n                    ┌─────▼─────┐\n                    │  Phase 2b │\n                    │  Parallel │\n                    └───────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component A] | None | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | B, C |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component B] | A | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | D |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component C] | A | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | D |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component D] | B, C | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Final] | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n<!-- FILL: Name the longest chain and its total. List what can run in parallel. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Implementation to verification, 40 minutes. Docs run in parallel. WEAK: The critical path is the main path. -->\n\n1. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n2. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n3. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Sum of durations]\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task A] and [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task B] can run simultaneously\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task C] and [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task D] can run after Phase 1\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n<!-- FILL: Name three milestones with a command-checkable success criterion. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: M1: the branch exists. `rg -n quiet` prints it. WEAK: Milestones are tracked. -->\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Setup Complete] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: All dependencies ready] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n| M2 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Core Done] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Main features working] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n| M3 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Release Ready] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: All tests pass] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n<!-- FILL: Write one ADR per decision. Name the context, the choice, the consequence and the rejected option. GOOD: ADR-001: a flag, because callers already pass flags. WEAK: We made a decision. -->\n\n### ADR-001: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Decision Title]\n\n**Status**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Proposed/Accepted/Deprecated]\n\n**Context**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What problem we're solving]\n\n**Decision**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What we decided]\n\n**Consequences**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Positive outcome 1]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Negative outcome + mitigation]\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Option B]: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Why rejected]\n\n---\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add a --quiet option to the recommend-level script's parser and one branch in its text renderer, so a caller gets the recommendation on one line while every existing invocation keeps its report.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2+ (`set -euo pipefail`) |\n| **Framework** | None - a standalone CLI script |\n| **Storage** | None |\n| **Testing** | Shell invocations, `bash -n`, `wc -l` and `diff` |\n\n### Overview\nThe change touches one script and adds about twenty lines. A `QUIET` global mirrors the existing `JSON_OUTPUT` flag, the parser gains a `--quiet` case, and `output_text()` returns after printing the recommendation line when quiet is set. Proof is a line count on both forms plus a byte diff against a captured baseline.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] `bash -n` clean and both output forms verified\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nOther: single-script branch. One script owns argument parsing, scoring and rendering; the change adds a branch to the existing renderer rather than a new output module.\n\n### Key Components\n- **Argument parser (`while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]` loop)**: Turns flags into globals; gains a `--quiet` case beside `--json`.\n- **`output_text()`**: Owns the human report; gains an early single-line return when quiet mode is active.\n- **`output_json()`**: Owns the machine document; unchanged, and still selected when `--json` is passed.\n\n### Data Flow\nArguments are parsed into globals, the score functions read those globals, and section 7 of the script dispatches to `output_json()` when `JSON_OUTPUT` is true and to `output_text()` otherwise. Quiet mode is read inside `output_text()` only, so the JSON path never sees it.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n\nThis is a feature, not a bug fix, but the script's stdout is a shared surface, so the producer/consumer inventory still applies.\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| `recommend-level.sh` `output_text()` | Producer of the human report | update - add the quiet branch | `rg -n 'QUIET' recommend-level.sh` names the branch |\n| `recommend-level.sh` `output_json()` | Producer of the machine document | unchanged - JSON wins over quiet | `bash recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2 --json --quiet \\| wc -l` prints 36 |\n| `show_help()` and the header usage block | Document the option surface | update - list `--quiet` | `bash recommend-level.sh --help \\| grep -c -- '--quiet'` prints 1 |\n| Callers in the spec-kit runtime and docs | Invoke the script with existing flags | not a consumer of the new flag; their invocations are unchanged | `rg -n 'recommend-level.sh' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit` still resolves, and no invocation passes `--quiet` |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `rg -n 'RECOMMEND_PHASES|JSON_OUTPUT' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` shows the two existing output globals the new one must match in shape.\n- Consumers of changed symbols: `rg -n 'output_text|output_json' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` lists the single dispatch site.\n- Matrix axes: inputs `--quiet` x `--json` x `--no-recommend-phases` = eight rows; the plan tests the four that differ.\n- Algorithm invariant: the recommendation line's text is `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)` in both modes; quiet changes the count of lines, never the line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | The quiet branch and the unchanged default branch of `output_text()` | `bash`, `wc -l`, `diff` |\n| Integration | `--quiet` combined with `--json` and `--no-recommend-phases`, plus the missing-input error path | `bash`, exit-status checks |\n| Manual | Read both forms once in a terminal to confirm the report still reads as before | Terminal |\n\nBaseline for the default form: `bash recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2` prints 16 lines today, with `Recommended Level: 0 (Quick)` on line 2. That output is captured to `scratch/baseline-default.txt` before the edit and diffed after it.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| `bash` 3.2+ | Internal | Green | The script cannot run; the requirement predates this change |\n| `diff` and `wc` | Internal | Green | Baseline comparison falls back to reading both outputs by hand |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\n- **Trigger**: The default report changes for any input, or `--quiet` prints more than one line.\n- **Procedure**: Revert the single commit that touches `recommend-level.sh`, then rerun the two baseline commands.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──────► Phase 2 (Implementation) ──────► Phase 3 (Verification)\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Implementation |\n| Implementation | Setup | Verification |\n| Verification | Implementation | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | Low | 10 minutes |\n| Core Implementation | Low | 20 minutes |\n| Verification | Low | 10 minutes |\n| **Total** | | **~40 minutes (assumption, not a commitment)** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [ ] Backup created (if data changes) - no data changes\n- [ ] Feature flag configured - the `--quiet` flag is per-invocation, not a rollout switch\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set - no service to monitor\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. Revert the commit that touches `recommend-level.sh`.\n2. Confirm the default form prints the baseline again: `bash recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2 | diff - scratch/baseline-default.txt` prints nothing.\n3. Confirm `--quiet` is gone: `bash recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet` exits 1 with `Unknown option`.\n4. Notify the packet's consumers only if the flag had already been published to them.\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** No\n- **Reversal procedure**: N/A - the script writes no data.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Setup     │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └──────┬──────┘     └─────────────┘\n                          │\n                    ┌─────▼─────┐\n                    │  Docs     │\n                    │  (T007)   │\n                    └───────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| Baseline capture (T002) | None | `scratch/baseline-default.txt` | T008 |\n| Parser change (T003, T004) | Baseline capture | `QUIET` global set by `--quiet` | T005 |\n| Renderer change (T005) | Parser change | The single-line output | T006, T008 |\n| Help text (T007) | Parser change | Documented option | T011 |\n| Verification (T008-T011) | Renderer, help text | Evidence for every AC row | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n\n1. **Baseline capture** - 5 minutes - CRITICAL\n2. **Parser and renderer change** - 20 minutes - CRITICAL\n3. **Verification** - 10 minutes - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: ~35 minutes\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- The help text (T007) can be written while the renderer change is reviewed.\n- The two documentation checks (T008, T009) can run independently once the code lands.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | Parser accepts the flag | `bash recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet` exits 0 | Phase 2 start |\n| M2 | Quiet renders one line | `bash recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet \\| wc -l` prints 1 | Phase 2 end |\n| M3 | Both forms verified | Default output diffs clean and every AC row is `Met` | Phase 3 end |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\n### ADR-001: Quiet as a text-renderer branch, not a global output mode\n\n**Status**: Proposed\n\n**Context**: The script has two output paths, `output_text()` and `output_json()`. A quiet flag could suppress both, or only the human report. Callers that pass `--json` already receive a machine-readable document, and replacing it with a single line would break their parsers.\n\n**Decision**: `--quiet` is read inside `output_text()` only. When `JSON_OUTPUT` is true the JSON path runs unchanged and quiet has no effect.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- A caller gets one line from the default path and an unchanged document from the JSON path; no caller loses output.\n- The flag's meaning depends on the other flag in play, which must be stated in the help text and pinned by a test.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Quiet suppressing JSON too: it would replace a parseable document with a non-JSON line, breaking the only consumers that asked for machine output.\n- A separate `--format=level` option: more surface for the same result, and the packet's scope is one flag.\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n## AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL\n\n### Pre-Task Checklist\n- [ ] Read the whole task line in `tasks.md`, including its `Verify:` clause.\n- [ ] Confirm the target file is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`; this packet changes no other source file.\n- [ ] Capture the baseline for the default form before editing.\n\n### Execution Rules\n\n| Rule | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| `TASK-SEQ` | Run tasks in numeric order; T008 depends on the T002 baseline. |\n| `TASK-SCOPE` | Touch `recommend-level.sh` only. A need to edit another file is a scope change to raise, not to absorb. |\n| `TASK-EVIDENCE` | Mark a task `[x]` only after its `Verify:` command printed the expected output. |\n\n### Status Reporting Format\nReport each task as `T### <done|blocked> - <the command run> -> <its output>`. A summary line reports the tasks completed, the tasks blocked and the next task.\n\n### Blocked Task Protocol\nMark the task `[B]` in `tasks.md`, write the blocking command and its output beneath it, and stop. Do not reorder around a blocked task: the verification chain assumes the earlier evidence exists.\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":96,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":81}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
